-- title:
--   Incomparable branch ideals at a crossing point
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ be a nonzero natural number and $q$ a prime not dividing $N_0$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of the structure `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O \colon$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to O$ whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ together with a ring homomorphism $t \colon O \to \kappa$. Let $n$ be a point of the scheme-theoretic fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔛.comp κ (t.comp ρO) 0` and `𝔛.comp κ (t.comp ρO) 1`, and let `𝔛.crossingPt ρO t n` be its image in `DRLevel.XO ρO` under the first projection followed by `𝔛.comp κ (t.comp ρO) 0` followed by `DRLevel.bcMap ρO t`. Assume that the two points `𝔛.ξinf ρO t` and `𝔛.ξzero ρO t` of `DRLevel.XO ρO` both specialise to this crossing point, with specialisation witnesses `hinf` and `hzero`. For such a specialisation $h \colon \xi \rightsquigarrow x$, `Scheme.branchIdeal h` denotes the ideal of the stalk at $x$ obtained by pulling back the maximal ideal of the stalk at $\xi$ along the induced map of stalks. The conclusion is that the two ideals `Scheme.branchIdeal hzero` and `Scheme.branchIdeal hinf` of the stalk at the crossing point are incomparable: neither is contained in the other.
--
--   At a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of level $(N_0,q)$ base changed to $O$, the two branches through the point are genuinely distinct, expressed as incomparability of the two associated branch ideals in the local ring at the point. The statement feeds the local analysis of such points, in particular the lower bound on the Krull dimension of the stalk, the production of oriented crossing charts, and the chart presentations of stalks used for the resolved model.
